    <!-- Which marketplace prices Pokémon, Magic and One Piece cards come from -->
    <string name="settings_price_source">Price source (Pokémon, Magic &amp; One Piece)</string>
    <string name="settings_price_source_hint">Cardmarket trend price for European prices, TCGplayer market price for US prices. For One Piece you pick the exact Cardmarket listing (set and V.1/V.2…) of your copy. The other games only have TCGplayer prices. When the two markets disagree by more than 3×, one of them is linked to the wrong card and the app uses the other one (the card shows a note). Graded cards use your own value; the card page links to recent sales.</string>
    <string name="settings_refresh_hint">Prices refresh automatically once a day, which also records the value history.</string>
    <string name="settings_refresh_now">Refresh prices now</string>
